# Line-ending policy.
#
# Many files in this repo are hashed byte-for-byte (protocol/ + shared-vectors/
# via scripts/freeze_protocol_hashes.sh --check, the vendored SQLite/SQLCipher
# amalgamations via libsqlite3-sys-raven/build.rs, the secret-service fork via
# node/scripts/verify_secret_service_2_0_2_raven_noprompt.sh) and the harness
# scripts are bash. With Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true an
# unmodified checkout would otherwise get CRLF: every hash would drift and
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash` scripts would stop running.
#
# Rules are applied top to bottom and the LAST matching rule wins, so the
# general rule comes first and the byte-pinned `-text` overrides come last.
# Existing index blobs are already LF, so this needs no renormalisation
# (verify with `git add --renormalize . && git status --short`).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.rs text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.lock text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
protocol/** text eol=lf
shared-vectors/** text eol=lf

# Task 0A.1 / 0A.2 / supply-chain pins — byte-pinned vendored sources and
# provenance files. SHA-256 must match on every host. Git must not convert
# CRLF on Windows. This covers the ordinary SQLite amalgamation
# (libsqlite3-sys-raven/sqlite3/**, hashed on every build by build.rs), the
# SQLCipher trees, and the vendored secret-service fork (which keeps one
# upstream CRLF file; -text stops a later renormalize from touching it).
node/third_party/** -text
node/third_party/sqlcipher-4.17.0/** -text
node/third_party/libsqlite3-sys-raven/sqlcipher/** -text
node/third_party/libsqlite3-sys-raven/sqlite3/** -text
